meta {
  name: list
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users?page=1&page_size=20
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.page_info.page: eq 1
  res.body.page_info.page_size: eq 20
}

docs {
  Listing requires the user:list permission, so a member gets 403 here.
  errors/users-forbidden.bru is that same request with a member token.

  A page past the end returns an empty items array with the real total, not
  a 404: asking for page 99999999 is a valid question with a boring answer.

  Query string is written inline in url: only. A params:query block was
  tried alongside it and mutation-tested with a different page_size value;
  the request actually sent, and the response, still used the value from
  url:, proving params:query is not honoured here when the same key is
  already in the url string. Keeping both would leave a block that looks
  editable but silently does nothing, so it is dropped.
}
